Chapter: UefiConsoleTest

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Works chapter UefiConsole

 UefiConsole wraps the firmware's text-in and text-out protocols. Most
 of it is decision rather than device: a key arrives as a scan code, a
 character code and a shift mask, and the chapter's job is to say which
 of forty-odd predicates that key satisfies. Attributes and pixels are
 the same shape of work -- packing named colours into the bit layout the
 firmware expects.

 The old body touched none of it. It cited UI Widget and UI Layout, not
 UefiConsole, built a menu of thirteen strings, and printed
 `selected=0` from a `sel-idx` bound to the literal 0 two lines above --
 an assertion whose answer was written in the assertion.

 What is NOT covered here, deliberately: uefi-console-init reads the
 SystemTable through peek-qword, and uefi-con-move and friends call into
 ConOut. Those need firmware, and a test that pretended otherwise would
 be reading whatever address zero happens to hold. This pins the half
 that is arithmetic, and says so rather than implying the chapter is
 covered.

Section: Key Fixtures

  uct-key : Integer, Integer, Integer -> UefiKey
  uct-key (scan) (ch) (shift) =
    UefiKey { scan-code = scan, char-code = ch, shift-state = shift }

  uct-ctrl : Integer = 8
  uct-alt : Integer = 32
  uct-valid : Integer = 2147483648

Section: Predicate Reporting

 Each key is described by the NAMES of every predicate it satisfies, not
 by a count. A count would pass if two predicates swapped which key they
 answered to; the names would not.

  uct-flag : Boolean, Text -> Text
  uct-flag (b) (name) = if b then name & " " else ""

  uct-describe : UefiKey -> Text
  uct-describe (k) =
    uct-flag (uefi-key-is-char k) "char"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-enter k) "enter"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-backspace k) "backspace"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-tab k) "tab"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-escape k) "escape"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-arrow-up k) "up"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-arrow-down k) "down"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-arrow-left k) "left"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-arrow-right k) "right"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-home k) "home"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-end k) "end"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-insert k) "insert"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-delete k) "delete"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-page-up k) "pgup"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-page-down k) "pgdn"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-has-shift k) "+shift"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-has-ctrl k) "+ctrl"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-has-alt k) "+alt"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-ctrl-c k) "ctrl-c"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-ctrl-s k) "ctrl-s"
    & uct-flag (uefi-key-is-ctrl-alt-del k) "ctrl-alt-del"

  uct-report : Text, UefiKey -> [Console] Nothing
  uct-report (label) (k) = print-line-uni (label & "=" & uct-describe k)

Section: Body

 The two ctrl-alt-delete lines are the point of the key half. They
 differ in one bit: the second omits the shift-state-valid flag, which
 the firmware sets to say the modifier bits mean anything at all. The
 predicate must answer no to the second, and a reboot combo that fires
 on an unset modifier field is exactly the failure worth pinning.

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    act
      uct-report "letter" (uct-key 0 97 0)
      uct-report "enter" (uct-key 0 13 0)
      uct-report "backspace" (uct-key 0 8 0)
      uct-report "tab" (uct-key 0 9 0)
      uct-report "escape" (uct-key uefi-scan-escape 0 0)
      uct-report "up" (uct-key uefi-scan-up 0 0)
      uct-report "down" (uct-key uefi-scan-down 0 0)
      uct-report "left" (uct-key uefi-scan-left 0 0)
      uct-report "right" (uct-key uefi-scan-right 0 0)
      uct-report "home" (uct-key uefi-scan-home 0 0)
      uct-report "end" (uct-key uefi-scan-end 0 0)
      uct-report "insert" (uct-key uefi-scan-insert 0 0)
      uct-report "delete" (uct-key uefi-scan-delete 0 0)
      uct-report "pgup" (uct-key uefi-scan-page-up 0 0)
      uct-report "pgdn" (uct-key uefi-scan-page-down 0 0)
      uct-report "shift-A" (uct-key 0 65 uefi-left-shift)
      uct-report "ctrl-c" (uct-key 0 3 uct-ctrl)
      uct-report "ctrl-s" (uct-key 0 19 uct-ctrl)
      uct-report "cad-valid" (uct-key uefi-scan-delete 0 (uct-valid + uct-ctrl + uct-alt))
      uct-report "cad-unvalidated" (uct-key uefi-scan-delete 0 (uct-ctrl + uct-alt))
      print-line-uni ("attr-yellow-on-blue=" & show (uefi-attr UefiYellow UefiBlue))
      print-line-uni ("attr-black-on-black=" & show (uefi-attr UefiBlack UefiBlack))
      print-line-uni ("attr-white-on-white=" & show (uefi-attr UefiWhite UefiWhite))
      print-line-uni ("pixel=" & show (uefi-pixel-pack (uefi-pixel 255 128 64)))
      print-line-uni ("pixel-black=" & show (uefi-pixel-pack (uefi-pixel 0 0 0)))
      print-line-uni ("char-31=" & show (uefi-key-is-char (uct-key 0 31 0)))
      print-line-uni ("char-32=" & show (uefi-key-is-char (uct-key 0 32 0)))
      print-line-uni ("char-126=" & show (uefi-key-is-char (uct-key 0 126 0)))
      print-line-uni ("char-127=" & show (uefi-key-is-char (uct-key 0 127 0)))
    end
